    <statement><p>Use the geometric definition of the cross product and the properties of the cross product to make the following calculations.</p>
<p>(a) <m>((\vec{i} + \vec{j}) \times \vec{i} ) \times \vec{j}</m> = <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>( \vec{j} + \vec{k} ) \times ( \vec{j} \times \vec{k} )</m> = <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>3 \vec{i} \times ( \vec{i} + \vec{j} )</m> = <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>(d) <m>( \vec{k} + \vec{j} ) \times ( \vec{k} - \vec{j} )</m> = <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;1,0,0\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;0,1,-1\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
